    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p17-obstinate-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "127 and 149.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p17-obstinate-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Subtract each smaller power of two: every remainder is composite. Each other odd number in the interval has at least one prime remainder.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The powers of two to test are $2,4,8,16,32,64,128$, stopping before a power exceeds the number.\n\nFor 127:\n$$\\begin{align*}127-2&=125=5\\times25\\\\127-4&=123=3\\times41\\\\127-8&=119=7\\times17\\\\127-16&=111=3\\times37\\\\127-32&=95=5\\times19\\\\127-64&=63=7\\times9\\end{align*}$$\nAll remainders are composite, and $128>127$.\n\nFor 149:\n$$\\begin{align*}149-2&=147=3\\times49\\\\149-4&=145=5\\times29\\\\149-8&=141=3\\times47\\\\149-16&=133=7\\times19\\\\149-32&=117=9\\times13\\\\149-64&=85=5\\times17\\\\149-128&=21=3\\times7\\end{align*}$$\nAll remainders are composite, and $256>149$.\n\nThe other 23 odd numbers are eliminated by these prime-plus-power-of-two representations:\n$$\\begin{align*}101&=97+4\\\\103&=101+2\\\\105&=103+2\\\\107&=103+4\\\\109&=107+2\\\\111&=109+2\\\\113&=109+4\\\\115&=113+2\\\\117&=113+4\\\\119&=103+16\\\\121&=113+8\\\\123&=107+16\\\\125&=109+16\\\\129&=127+2\\\\131&=127+4\\\\133&=131+2\\\\135&=131+4\\\\137&=73+64\\\\139&=137+2\\\\141&=139+2\\\\143&=139+4\\\\145&=137+8\\\\147&=139+8\\end{align*}$$\nThus the two obstinate numbers are 127 and 149.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
